nodecode-agentplaybooks is a rewrite of matebenyovszky's matebenyovszky/agentplaybooks:

  https://github.com/matebenyovszky/agentplaybooks
  commit f31e9c3af6520cebda1c0712447b4b487ffc12a7
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 AgentPlaybooks (LICENSE)

The original is one Hermes Agent plugin folder -- plugin.json, a README and the
skills/agentplaybooks-tools/SKILL.md prose skill -- holding no code of its own.
This rewrite keeps that skill's guidance as its (help :agentplaybooks) topic and
turns the commands the skill asks a host agent to type by hand into four tools
(apb_doctor, apb_setup, apb_connect, apb_project) and a /apb command, so the
cell builds the argv, keeps the profile selection on every call, defaults to a
preview and writes nothing without apply. It shells out to the same
AgentPlaybooks CLI, which the user installs themselves; the JSON manifest, the
README and the skill's frontmatter are prose with nothing to run, so they are
not carried. The CLI's own behaviour -- the writes into a harness profile and
the hosted calls -- stays in the CLI, exactly as in the original.
